## Fine-tuning Procedure: Overview

In principle, GPT-3 is capable of doing any NLP task, because everything is contained in the next token distribution. However, if we ask the model to generate a modern English sonnet, it will not do so correctly, because the model is only trained to predict the next word. Therefore, we need to somehow guide the large language model in order to fulfil specific tasks.

At first glance, it looks like training as usual, but it seems like the parameters have been chosen in a very specific way, so I will go through the fine tuning process for large language models. I might need to include some maths here, even though I think that higher level explanation is better suited for the general overview/section overview.

Fine tuning it's about generating training data which consists of at least the question and the answer to the question. Then the training data is put through a transformer, which generate numbers for the dot product. The model is trained using teacher-force learning, if we present two tokens then we want the next token to be the third token in our input "This is an example sentence." is the input, we would expect the token of "example" to be most likely. The model is trained with gradient descent and backpropagation.

