The purpose of HF transformers library is to help user derive the average model for the coupled inductors in his system. In addition, the library also allows you to include the information regarding the winding resistances and parasitic capacitances, so as to achieve the most accurate results. All the parameters required for the accurate modelling of losses in the transformer can be calculated using HF transformer library.

What is the advantage of using switched HF transformers?

A switched HF transformer can help provide voltage gain. The advantage of using a switched HF transformer over a rectifier is that you no longer need to have almost equal input and output voltage. You can now achieve higher efficiency using a smaller magnetics element.

You can give parasitic capacitances as well as resistance of your inductor to HF transformer library.

Yes, you can. In fact, the capacitances can be entered directly in Farads and so can the resistances be entered in Ohms. This makes the parameter deck more intuitive. The double-click shortcut also makes the calculations more user-friendly.

What is the difference between switching technology and resonant technology

A switched resonant transformer gives you smaller transformers, with less circulating current and no problem with DC biasing of the magnetics element. Power supply can be built without electrolytic capacitors and also with the use of completely surface mountable components.

Which switching of technique is better, voltage based or current based?

In most cases, you need to use the current mode for switching. Voltage-based switching circuits have faster transient response and simpler to design. But their noise immunity is bad as they have no fixed switching frequency.
