 HERE's Jonna Kultanen and Martin Sheridan from Product Marketing explain

A predictive algorithm logic is also referred to as a forecasting model. Developing such optimized inference models is always based on a specific client’s data. Models can be built in or out of product from HERE AI peers. The inference models leverage a unique dataset to maximize the predictive performance of specific algorithms, such as neural networks. It is also beneficial for individual companies to run inference behind the firewall by leveraging existing software, security & infrastructure. This also enables a compliance-based framework that complies with regulations surrounding data security and privacy constraints. The HERE platform provides a highly effective way of enabling streaming inference.

## Streaming data inference example

Uptime management is a critical aspect for any fleet, particularly if the fleet is supporting quick commerce logistics or servicing industries such as healthcare or retail. Optimizing the in-vehicle performance requires ongoing visibility into the customer vehicle availability, maintenance and repair status. To minimize unplanned downtime, it is important to get timely insight into the potential health issues associated with key components.

Streaming inference enables a continuous flow of data from a network of urban connected vehicles, including data collected on any sensors that are related to data from certain components (brakes, battery, tire pressure, etc.), or the vehicle’s operating status or behavior such as low feed and gear options to name a few. The platform enables a timely flow of data to inference models provided by the fleet provider or automotive OEM, to assist with optimizing vehicle diagnostics. This gives fleet managers’ added visibility into potential component performance issues and plan appropriate actions to resolve issues that could result in vehicle downtime.

This is a proactive and predictive approach to fleet maintenance and repair. Behind a firewall or within the HERE platform, inference model logic continuously assesses vehicle sensor data for component failures or performance issues, detect anomalies and then recommend optimized maintenance or repair activities, to reduce downtime.

## How HERE AI peers can help

Whatever the use case, a machine learning-powered inference model is based on a unique data set augmented by external datasets. This model can be provided by a 3 rd party (e.g., a HERE AI peer) or built in-house, depending on where the customer believes the predictive analytics brain is best located. The models can be effectively executed behind the firewall or within the HERE platform.

At HERE we take privacy very seriously. We understand how important privacy is to both your business and end-users, and we are committed to helping you earn and maintain their trust. Depending on the use-case, Beyond the core privacy features in the HERE Platform, privacy engineered capabilities can be provided to support a systematic and diverse set of techniques to ensure the data is kept private and secure.

Find out more on HERE AI peers and how it can help build mutually beneficial AI partnerships and improve digital experiences.

