    Cache is necessary for text generation, for example:

   ```python
from modeling_tf_bert import TFBertModel
generator = TFBertModel(config, return_dict=True)
generator.generate(prompts)
   ```

    In the inference phase, when a transformer generates text, it can cache the keys and values that are constant between different logical steps, so that we can reuse the kv-cache from the previous generation and exit in after generating as many tokens as we want. That allows us to not need to recompute those KV again, and that's the main reason why caching gives us a significant improvement in task efficiency. KV means the key and value embeddings that are computed by the model. Note that not all models use KV so only some models in the Model Family support this feature.

