 Can we use it to develop something?

Three days ago, Meta AI introduced a new version of its revolutionary AI model LLaMA. It is called LLaMA 2. To promote it as an open technology, LLaMA will be free for researchers and other interested parties. But the company does not recommend immediate use for business applications.

“The LLaMA 2 licence for publication explicitly reserves the right to use the model and training dataset in the development of commercial products.” – representatives said at the presentation.

LLaMA 2 is already available for download and experimentation in Meta GrusAI. The full and open LLaMA 2 model is available in a 7 billion and a 13 billion parameter version. The cached 70 billion parameter model, which requires users to have a GPU with at least 48GB of VRAM and more or less 1 TB of SSD storage to run, is also available.

While training LLaMA 2, AI developers tried to avoid any copyright materials. For example, the authors did not use Reddit or Common Crawl. Still, due to the lack of control over the millions of used pages, the company cannot guarantee that LLaMA 2 is not ‘poisoned’.

Given the lack of strict safety guarantees, Meta does not recommend end users to use ChatLLaMA or WebChatLLaMA, two implementations of the model that resemble ChatGPT.

The authors themselves admit that their model may still suffer from ‘frequent’ hallucinations – a distortion of the truth when generating text. The model also sometimes generates non-viable answers. For example, when asked where the entrance to the gymnasium is, LLaMA 2 can answer that it is next to the entrance to the supermarket. Granted, in this case the hallucination is more noticeable, but in other cases, due to the high quality of language, it can be more difficult to notice.

However, there is no need to write off the model right away. Here’s what Meta representatives have to say about it:

“We adhere to one overarching goal: to enable sustainable and responsible use of the LLaMA models. Safety is vital at every stage of model development – from research and development to release. If done right, safety veils any model, including LLaMA 2, bringing infinite benefits to all of us.”

If you need to create any AI app or device, our team is ready to assist you. Get in touch with us via email hi@unboxed.ai.
