Lets first assume that we have no attention - that simply means someone can not build an attention graph.  You simply cannot rely on the social graph, because the social graph focuses most prominently on humans who are merely nodes in the system - the fact is, chatbots can be great prefer friends in chat among themselves.  The other issue, is that there is no attention hacking that we can do since everyone will be able to pay attention to everything just at different times. We will never see a game where someone becomes a high-degree-node (BDN) who has the power to manipulate the market.  We have a system where each target will pay attention to everything simply at different times.

Now lets figure out what attention is and what it’s not.  Then we will talk about ways to represent this information and then how to use it to predict reward.

Attention is a fundamental ingredient to all analytics and not to be confused with the vanity metrics that people say are indicative of attention such as:

- Likes, upvotes or re-tweets
- Page views
- Webinar attendance
- Unique email addresses
- Tweets/posts focusing on brand tags
- Tweets/posts mentioning positive brand-related phrases
- Impressions or ad views
