If you want to optimise your deep learning models for performance at the edge, then you might want to use Triton Inference Server, now available from Source Code Control in the Node-RED Contrib Library.

Triton offers:

- High utilization through concurrent execution and pipeline execution of GPU inference requests
- High throughput due to large batch sizes using batcher and a backlog queue
- Enables near-real-time inference service levels through a Kubernetes Autoscaler based on custom inference metrics supplied by NVIDIA Triton
- Model snapshotting to improve start-up latency
- Model ensemble inference chaining through model configuration
- Dynamic model configuration reloads without inference interruptions

These features are accessible through a single common client API or (gRPC) over HTTP/2 endpoint accessible from any hardware platform and programming language.

How to use Inference Node in your flows

Inference Node helps reduce code writing time and allows you to experiment with predictive services based on trained deep learning models, as deployed into Triton Inference Server.

Supported model sources include:

- TensorFlow (TensorFlow) EN
- TensorFlow (TensorFlow 2.0) EN
- TensorFlow/TensorRT (TensorFlow) EN
- TensorFlow (TensorFlow SavedModel) EN
- Custom C++ EN
- PyTorch EN
- Process EN
