- ONNX (TensorFlow) (*experimental) EN
- RNG EN
- FILTER GRPC EN
- Core ML (Apple) EN
- TensorFlow Lite (Google/Android) EN
- MXNet EN

Inference Node is the way to access predictive deep learning models as instances of the Triton Inference Server. It provides the output of the predictive operation from the data passed as input.

You can design Node-RED applications that access predictive deep learning models quickly and easily, by running a Triton Inference Server (TRITON), enabling your users to interact with deep learning endpoints in TRITON using Node-RED flows.

Once you have opened your Inference Node settings page, you can then define the details of the Triton Inference Server, the model and any inputs and outputs for the model. This will include the different information for representations of each piece of data, and some deep learning model applications require an array of vectors, rather than a string.

You can select the required model representation based on the Image, Text, Audio or User defined data.

