Latency is a measure of the "delay" in the model's predictions: how much of a delay is there between the time the models sees its input and time it makes its prediction.

More formally, it is the time between the model's window start and the output's target timestamp. As an example, given a model with a window start of 2017-02-10 and a window end of 2017-02-13, running once a day, predicting values of 2017-02-11, 2017-02-12, and 2017-02-13 would have latency 0 days, 1 day, and 2 days respectively.

