Windows global OS parameters
1. Memory parameters defaults 806 MB are not at all optimized for real systems, set it to 8 Gb or at least 2 Gb
2. Windows 10 likes to suspend and hibernate processes , nice. So Disable sleep and hibernate
3. Disable file history and OneDrive
4. Disable IPv6
5. configure power settings to High Performance.
6. configure networking buffers
7. configure disk /CPU priority

MySql database server Configuration:
1. disable unused engines
2. optimize data directory (xfs)
3. optimize tmp directory
4. make mysql_upgrade for ALL databases
5. enable query cache and prepare some parameters
6. optimize my.ini (support, Percona Xtrabackup, …)
7. Disable OFF privileges
8. enable semi-sync plugin and performance-schema use PFS-Xtrabackup , ensure transaction safety
9. disable binary logs (not needed for replication)
10. optimize timestamps
11. use gen_rand_alias for primary keys to avoid sequential scanning
13. many many options in https://www.percona.com/system-configuration-mysql
14. rename Windows mysql process to less obvious

