- generation_config.json contains settings for generating Named Data Language (NDL) code from models that were imported from Open Travel Standard (OTS).
- config.json indicates the version of the compiler that was used to compile the schema.

- NDL is a an open source domain-specific language, created to ease definition of interoperable APIs that can be used to create messages.
- NDL is a feature-rich language that implements pattern-based serialization and deserialization for JSON, XML and binary formats.
- OTS to NDL code generation is enabled using generation_config.json.
- Downloaded JSON files from the server will have the generation_config.json file.
- generation_config.json is required to convert any OTS model to NDL model using either of the following methods:

(A) Using the ‘generate’ functionality within Pandera.

(B) Using the Open Source NDL Compiler of Avinor.

- At any point, the user can modify generation_config.json and implement the changes to their project.
- generation_config.json is only required to convert OTS to NDL. After conversion, the user has complete control to edit NDL files.
- While importing any future OTS release, generation_config.json can be uploaded back to the server and this will give the user the ability to import future OTS releases to existing code.
