Airdrops have become an industry standard helping to generate a good number of tokens over time. They often lack the level of price discovery at initial Coin offerings.  This reduces the free market’s capacity to sway the initial price of the token price and to a certain degree, expectations.

Decentralized applications tend to require consumers on an intrinsic level, hence addressing the network effect problem that occurs when it comes to app implementation.

With each token being traded, its conversions on the Bancor network bring about increased liquidity to the DApp users.

The smart contract gives actual clarity on the earned level of liquidity in BNT to the application operators.

The reward gives a network effect to the decentralized application hence increasing efficiency.

